  "headline": "94.4% of a real 6960-factor LLM pool is killed by the universal |t|<1.96 hurdle (median |t|=0.71) -- the diagnostic that the hurdle discards at massive scale.",
  "honest_verdict_part_b": "On a 35-factor formulaic LLM-STYLE battery built on A-shares, 69% are discarded by the universal hurdle, but after a causal sign-fix the discarded book is ~0 (SR -0.30) and coarse reallocation does NOT revive it (lift -0.11). Lesson, stated plainly in the paper: venue salvage revives factors that carry REAL content misallocated across venues (US OSAP: +0.45; A-share classic anomalies: +0.95 coarse), NOT arbitrary noise. A random price/volume formulaic zoo's discards can be genuinely empty. Salvage is a resolution correction, not alchemy -- this boundary is a feature of the theory, not a failure."
}
